# nebio fast GPIO, on the configsettings page of the instr selector.
# A .ui entry is not run as a program: Nebulae itself handles it (ui.py,
# mode = the name after the number, here "nebio_fast_gpio").
# Speed click on it: on/off, and back to the instrument. On: nebio reads the
# buttons, encoders and polled gates straight from the GPIO registers
# (/dev/gpiomem, Pi 1-4) instead of through libgpiod's system calls: a little
# less CPU (about 2 % of one core on a Pi 4). Checked against libgpiod first;
# if the check fails it stays off. Off (default): libgpiod. Saved
# (configsettings.py).
# Slot LED bright = on (nebulae-status).
